('CIT_ASCLEPIUS_HH','ENT_ASCLEPIUS','SRC_HOMERIC_HYMNS','Homeric Hymn 16','lines 1-4','I begin to sing of Asclepius, son of Apollo and healer of sicknesses. In the Dotian plain fair Coronis, daughter of King Phlegyas, bare him, a great joy to men, a soother of cruel pangs. (l. 5) And so hail to you, lord: in my song I make my prayer to thee!','Hugh G. Evelyn-White',1914,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/348','primary-verbatim',NULL,DATE '2026-06-17','deterministic verbatim extraction + substring gate (Gutenberg #348)',1),
