('CIT_PLOUTON_HH','ENT_PLOUTON','SRC_HOMERIC_HYMNS','Homeric Hymn 18','lines 1-9','I sing of Cyllenian Hermes, the Slayer of Argus, lord of Cyllene and Arcadia rich in flocks, luck-bringing messenger of the deathless gods. He was born of Maia, the daughter of Atlas, when she had made with Zeus,-a shy goddess she.','Hugh G. Evelyn-White',1914,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/348','primary-verbatim',NULL,DATE '2026-06-17','deterministic verbatim extraction + substring gate (Gutenberg #348)',1),
